---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CHECKED_ON, u, affiliateProviders } from '../site.js';
const aff = affiliateProviders();
---
<Base title="Affiliate disclosure" description="How Get Paid From Anywhere may earn money from links, which links are affiliate links today, and how that does and does not affect what we publish." crumb="Affiliate disclosure">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <p class="meta"><span class="chip">Last updated {CHECKED_ON}</span></p>
    <h2>Which links are affiliate links</h2>
    {aff.length === 0
      ? <p><strong>None today.</strong> Every provider link on this site goes to the provider's normal website, and we earn nothing if you sign up.</p>
      : <><p>These providers' "Visit" links are affiliate links. They are marked with <code>rel="sponsored"</code> and a label next to the link:</p><ul>{aff.map((p) => <li><a href={u(`/provider/${p.slug}/`)}>{p.name}</a></li>)}</ul></>}
    <h2>How it would work</h2>
    <p>Some links on this site may become affiliate or referral links. If you sign up through one, we may earn a commission or referral fee at no extra cost to you. Affiliate links are labeled where they appear and listed on this page.</p>
    <h2>What affiliate deals do not change</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Country rules and fees come from the providers' own pages, whatever the deal.</li>
      <li>A provider without an affiliate program is listed the same way as one with a program.</li>
      <li>We do not accept payment to change a status label or the order of a table.</li>
      <li>If a provider asks us to remove an accurate, sourced fact, we keep the fact and drop the link.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Questions about this policy: see the <a href={u('/about/')}>About</a> page.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
